Subject: [PATCH 079/230] Debug Telegram login, serve A-ADS as raw HTML, cut
 the tab bar to three
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three fixes for the reported issues:

- Telegram Guest login: the auth_date freshness window is TEMP-bypassed (an
  out-of-window payload is now logged instead of rejected) to isolate whether
  the clock is why "Continue as <Name>" lands as a Guest; the verify suite pins
  the temporary acceptance and moves with verify.ts when the window is re-armed.
- A-ADS: the verifier does not run JavaScript and could not see the React
  banner ("Not found"), so the unit is raw HTML in index.html, intentionally
  ungated by ADS_ENABLED so a no-JS crawler still sees it.
- Bottom nav: Browse and Table leave the bar (five tabs crowded a 360px
  webview); the Matchday feed carries them as two shortcuts. Routes unchanged.

